# Signers trusted for `git log --show-signature` / `git verify-commit`.
# Format: <principal> [options] <key-type> <key>
# namespaces="git" restricts this key to git signatures, so it cannot be
# used to satisfy verification for other ssh-signed payloads.
#
# Only the personal identity is listed. Work commits are signed as well —
# bitbucket remotes pull in ~/.gitconfig-work, which carries its own 1Password
# signingkey — but that key and the address it belongs to stay out of this repo,
# like the rest of the work identity. That file points gpg.ssh.allowedSignersFile
# at ~/.gitconfig-work-signers instead, so this file is never the one consulted
# in a work repo.
kenny@kennyb.dev namespaces="git" ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIOISHjId1mlt/MUYsl1rA/J8ox77BFvqQL7e8dZWWvc5
